{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:InformationTheory.QuantumComputationalUniversality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"InformationTheory.QuantumComputationalUniversality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumComputationalUniversality.QuantumComputationalUniversality.information_content","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumComputationalUniversality.QuantumComputationalUniversality.information_content","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-computational-universality.lean#L87-L87","doc":"Sub-claim (4): information content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumComputationalUniversality.QuantumComputationalUniversality.descent_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumComputationalUniversality.QuantumComputationalUniversality.descent_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-computational-universality.lean#L85-L85","doc":"Sub-claim (3): descent decomposition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumComputationalUniversality.QuantumComputationalUniversality.universality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumComputationalUniversality.QuantumComputationalUniversality.universality","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-computational-universality.lean#L83-L83","doc":"Sub-claim (2): quantum universality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumComputationalUniversality.QuantumComputationalUniversality.quadratic_level","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumComputationalUniversality.QuantumComputationalUniversality.quadratic_level","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-computational-universality.lean#L81-L81","doc":"Sub-claim (1): quadratic level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumComputationalUniversality.QuantumComputationalUniversality.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumComputationalUniversality.QuantumComputationalUniversality.mk","kind":"ctor","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-computational-universality.lean#L79-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumComputationalUniversality.QuantumComputationalUniversality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumComputationalUniversality.QuantumComputationalUniversality","kind":"class","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-computational-universality.lean#L75-L87","doc":"**Quantum computational universality conjecture** (axiomatised\nas a class per AGENTS.md §3b-cond). Each field corresponds to\none of the four sub-claims; downstream blocks may take\n`[QuantumComputationalUniversality]` as a class hypothesis. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:quantum-computational-universality","label":"conj:quantum-computational-universality","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-computational-universality.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumComputationalUniversality.InformationContentHolds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumComputationalUniversality.InformationContentHolds","kind":"opaque","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-computational-universality.lean#L69-L73","doc":"**Sub-claim (4): information content**.\n\nOpaque Prop. The Skein polynomial encodes up to `c² − 1`\ncoefficients, the factored form compresses to `O(c)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumComputationalUniversality.DescentDecompositionHolds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumComputationalUniversality.DescentDecompositionHolds","kind":"opaque","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-computational-universality.lean#L62-L67","doc":"**Sub-claim (3): descent decomposition**.\n\nOpaque Prop. At the root-of-unity level, `End(V⊗n)` decomposes\ninto the descended (classical) subalgebra and the transient\n(quantum) complement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumComputationalUniversality.QuantumUniversalityHolds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumComputationalUniversality.QuantumUniversalityHolds","kind":"opaque","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-computational-universality.lean#L53-L60","doc":"**Sub-claim (2): quantum universality (FKLW)**.\n\nOpaque Prop. At level `k ≥ 3`, the braiding representation is\ndense in `SU(2^n)`; every quantum circuit on `n` qubits with\n`N` gates approximates within `ε` via a braid of\n`c = O(N polylog(1/ε))` crossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumComputationalUniversality.QuadraticLevelHolds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumComputationalUniversality.QuadraticLevelHolds","kind":"opaque","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-computational-universality.lean#L46-L51","doc":"**Sub-claim (1): quadratic level**.\n\nOpaque Prop. For a braid with `c = 3N` crossings, there exists\na root of unity at level `k ≥ 3` with `k + 2 ≤ c² − 1` such\nthat the Skein polynomial does not vanish at `q_k`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}